FOIHireloom PostgreSQL migrations

Run from the project root, using DATABASE_URL from the environment or .env:

  uv run --locked alembic -c src/FOIHireloom/db/alembic/alembic.ini upgrade head
  uv run --locked alembic -c src/FOIHireloom/db/alembic/alembic.ini current
  uv run --locked alembic -c src/FOIHireloom/db/alembic/alembic.ini check

Create a new revision after changing ORM models:

  uv run --locked alembic -c src/FOIHireloom/db/alembic/alembic.ini revision --autogenerate -m "describe schema change"

Review generated operations, including upgrade and downgrade, before committing.
Each migration belongs in a separate commit. Revisions contain fixed schema
operations and must not import current application models.

Preview SQL without connecting:

  uv run --locked alembic -c src/FOIHireloom/db/alembic/alembic.ini upgrade head --sql

Revert the latest revision:

  uv run --locked alembic -c src/FOIHireloom/db/alembic/alembic.ini downgrade -1

Downgrades can remove tables and their data. Use a disposable database when
testing upgrade/downgrade cycles. Schema migrations do not run on MCP startup.

The async connection lifecycle is encapsulated in MigrationEnvironment in env.py. For
programmatic use inside an async application, pass a synchronous connection
through Config.attributes["connection"] from AsyncConnection.run_sync().

Reference structure

This directory follows:
https://github.com/anmarkoulis/layered-architecture/tree/main/src/layered_architecture/db/alembic

  alembic/
    README
    alembic.ini
    env.py
    script.py.mako
    versions/
      <revision>_<description>.py

As in the reference, env.py owns the offline and online migration paths,
uses Base.metadata for autogeneration, bridges async connections with run_sync,
uses NullPool, and enables transaction_per_migration. MigrationEnvironment
encapsulates these operations as methods to follow this project's OOP convention.

Project-specific differences:
- alembic.ini resolves script_location relative to its own location with %(here)s,
  so commands work from the repository root; logging is configured in this file
  because Settings does not provide the reference project's LOGGING_CONFIG.
- DATABASE_URL goes directly to create_async_engine/context.configure to preserve
  percent-encoded passwords without ConfigParser interpolation.
- Type/default comparisons, disposal in finally, and an optionally supplied
  connection are retained for schema checks, cleanup, and async integration tests.
- Celery's include_object filter is omitted because this project has no Celery
  tables. The revision template retains type annotations on standard Alembic hooks.
